POWER & BASELINES
-----------------
[BAT+]----[FUSE]----+-------------------------------+
                    |                               |
                   [RSENSE]                         |
                    |                               |
                   NODE_I                           |
                                                   GND
[BAT-]------------------------------------------------+


======================================================================================
1. COLD-START DELAY (TRANSISTOR-LEVEL)
======================================================================================

[BAT+]----[RCH] 100kΩ----+---- NODE_DELAY
                         |
                        [CDELAY] 10µF
                         |
                        GND

NODE_DELAY → Q1 (NPN inverter):

   Q1:
     - Collector: DELAY_OK
     - Base: NODE_DELAY via R1
     - Emitter: GND

DELAY_OK ----[RDK]----> ENABLE_WINDOW


======================================================================================
2. MULTI-SENSOR MATRIX (TRANSISTOR-LEVEL LOGIC)
======================================================================================

SENSORS:
  NODE_I    (from RSENSE)
  NODE_TH   (NTC hotspot)
  NODE_CASE (NTC enclosure)
  NODE_AIR  (airflow sensor)

COMPARATORS (IC blocks):
  U_I    : NODE_I vs I_REF_MAX   → I_FAULT
  U_TH   : NODE_TH vs T_REF_HOT  → TH_FAULT
  U_CASE : NODE_CASE vs T_REF_CASE → CASE_FAULT
  U_AIR  : NODE_AIR vs AIR_MIN   → AIR_FAULT

OR NETWORK (discrete):

  I_FAULT ----[R2]----> base Q2A (NPN)
  TH_FAULT ---[R3]----> base Q2B (NPN)
  CASE_FAULT -[R4]----> base Q2C (NPN)
  AIR_FAULT --[R5]----> base Q2D (NPN)

  Q2A, Q2B, Q2C, Q2D:
    - Emitters: GND
    - Collectors tied together → NODE_OR

NODE_OR → Q2 (NPN buffer):

  Q2:
    - Collector: FAULT_LINE
    - Base: NODE_OR via R6
    - Emitter: GND


======================================================================================
3. THERMAL HYSTERESIS BLOCK (TRANSISTOR-LEVEL LATCH)
======================================================================================

COMPARATORS:
  U_HI : NODE_TH vs T_HIGH_REF → HOT_FAULT
  U_LO : NODE_TH vs T_LOW_REF  → COOL_OK

HOT_FAULT → Q3 (NPN set driver):

  Q3:
    - Collector: HYST_SET_NODE
    - Base: HOT_FAULT via R7
    - Emitter: GND

COOL_OK → Q4 (NPN reset driver):

  Q4:
    - Collector: HYST_RESET_NODE
    - Base: COOL_OK via R8
    - Emitter: GND

SR LATCH (cross-coupled NPN pair):

  QH_SET (NPN):
    - Collector: HYST_LATCH_OUT
    - Base: HYST_SET_NODE via R9 and feedback from QH_RESET collector via R10
    - Emitter: GND

  QH_RESET (NPN):
    - Collector: HYST_LATCH_BAR
    - Base: HYST_RESET_NODE via R11 and feedback from QH_SET collector via R12
    - Emitter: GND

HYST_LATCH_OUT → HYST_FAULT


======================================================================================
4. MASTER SAFETY LATCH (TRANSISTOR-LEVEL)
======================================================================================

FAULT_LINE ----[R13]----> base Q5 (NPN)
HYST_FAULT ----[R14]----> base Q5 (wired-OR via resistors)

Q5 (NPN set driver):
  - Collector: MASTER_SET_NODE
  - Base: from R13/R14 node
  - Emitter: GND

RESET_SW ----[R15]----> base Q6 (NPN)

Q6 (NPN reset driver):
  - Collector: MASTER_RESET_NODE
  - Base: RESET_SW via R15
  - Emitter: GND

MASTER SR LATCH:

  QM_SET (NPN):
    - Collector: MASTER_FAULT_OUT
    - Base: MASTER_SET_NODE via R16 and feedback from QM_RESET collector via R17
    - Emitter: GND

  QM_RESET (NPN):
    - Collector: MASTER_FAULT_BAR
    - Base: MASTER_RESET_NODE via R18 and feedback from QM_SET collector via R19
    - Emitter: GND

MASTER_FAULT_OUT → GLOBAL_SHUTDOWN


======================================================================================
5. GLOBAL SHUTDOWN & INDICATORS (TRANSISTOR-LEVEL)
======================================================================================

GLOBAL_SHUTDOWN:
  MASTER_FAULT_OUT ----> GLOBAL_SHUTDOWN (logic node)

LED drivers:

  MATRIX_FAULT ----[RLED1]----> base QLED1 (NPN)
  HYST_FAULT   ----[RLED2]----> base QLED2 (NPN)
  MASTER_FAULT_OUT ----[RLED3]----> base QLED3 (NPN)

  QLED1, QLED2, QLED3:
    - Collectors: respective LED anodes
    - Emitters: GND
    - LED cathodes to supply via resistors (or vice versa, depending on polarity)


======================================================================================
6. TAMA ENGINE — DISCRETE MCU CORE (TRANSISTOR-LEVEL)
======================================================================================

BUTTON DEBOUNCE & PULSE:

  [BTN_OP]----+------------------------[RPU] 10kΩ----+---- 5V
              |                                      |
             [C1] 100nF                             Q7 (NPN)
              |                                      |
             GND                                   NODE_OP

  Q7:
    - Collector: NODE_OP
    - Base: BTN_OP via R20
    - Emitter: GND

POTENTIOMETER & COMPARATOR LADDER:

  [POT] top ---- 5V
  [POT] wiper --+----> NODE_ANALOG
  [POT] bottom - GND

  NODE_ANALOG --[R21]--+--[R22]--+--[R23]--+--[R24]-- GND
                        |        |        |
                       Q8       Q9       Q10
                        |        |        |
                      BIT0     BIT1     BIT2

  Q8, Q9, Q10:
    - Bases: taps along ladder
    - Collectors: BIT0/1/2 nodes
    - Emitters: GND

ADD/SUB MODE:

  [SW_MODE]----[RMS] 10kΩ---- 5V
               |
              Q11 (NPN) → NODE_MODE

  Q11:
    - Collector: NODE_MODE
    - Base: SW_MODE via RMS
    - Emitter: GND

XOR GATES FOR TWO’S COMPLEMENT (per bit):

  For each BITn:

    BITn ----> XOR gate with NODE_MODE:

    XOR gate (4 × NPN: QX1–QX4):

      QX1, QX2, QX3, QX4:
        - Arranged in standard transistor XOR topology:
          SUMn = BITn ⊕ NODE_MODE
        - Output: BITn'

FULL ADDERS (FA0–FA3):

  Each FAx uses:
    - XOR gates (4 × NPN)
    - AND gates (2 × NPN)
    - OR gate (2 × NPN)

  Inputs:
    A = ACCx (previous)
    B = BITx' (operand)
    Cin = carry from previous stage

  Outputs:
    SUMx → FFx D input
    Coutx → next FA carry input

FLIP-FLOPS (FF0–FF3):

  Each FFx is a master–slave latch pair:

    Master latch:
      QF_M1, QF_M2 (NPN pair)
        - Cross-coupled
        - D input from SUMx
        - Clock from NODE_OP

    Slave latch:
      QF_S1, QF_S2 (NPN pair)
        - Cross-coupled
        - Driven by master
        - Outputs ACCx

CLOCK DISTRIBUTION:

  NODE_OP ----[RCLK] 1kΩ----> bases of all FF master latch transistors (QF_M1..M4)

OUTPUT LEDs:

  ACC0 ----[RLED4]----> base QOUT0 (NPN)
  ACC1 ----[RLED5]----> base QOUT1 (NPN)
  ACC2 ----[RLED6]----> base QOUT2 (NPN)
  ACC3 ----[RLED7]----> base QOUT3 (NPN)

  QOUT0–QOUT3:
    - Collectors: LED anodes
    - Emitters: GND
    - LED cathodes to supply via resistors (or inverted, depending on design)


======================================================================================
TRANSISTOR COUNT (APPROXIMATE, EDUCATIONAL)
======================================================================================

- Cold-start:        1 × NPN (Q1)
- Matrix OR + buffer: 5 × NPN (Q2A–D, Q2)
- Hysteresis latch:   4 × NPN (Q3, Q4, QH_SET, QH_RESET)
- Master latch:       4 × NPN (Q5, Q6, QM_SET, QM_RESET)
- LED drivers:        3 × NPN (QLED1–3)
- Button + pot front-end: 4 × NPN (Q7, Q8–Q10)
- Mode + XOR + adders + FFs: dozens of NPNs (gate + latch network)
- Output drivers:     4 × NPN (QOUT0–3)

Total: on the order of **50–100 NPN transistors** for the full logic + safety backplane.

